  "created": "2026-11-01T13:38:25.557Z",
  "description": "EVO HTML to PDF Library for .NET (Classic API on the Next Engine, Windows ARM64) runs the Classic EvoPdf API on the Chromium-based rendering engine of EvoPdf Next. It converts HTML to PDF and creates PDF documents in .NET applications on Windows ARM64 with the EvoPdf namespace (HtmlToPdfConverter, Document, PdfPage, the elements, templates, forms, bookmarks and security settings) and renders modern HTML, CSS and JavaScript as EvoPdf Next does.\n\nAn application written for the EvoPdf.HtmlToPdf package keeps its code and changes only the package reference. The license key is set as before. Each converter gives access to the EvoPdf Next converter it uses, for the options the EvoPdf API has no setting for, such as the PDF standard.\n\nThis package installs the Windows ARM64 runtime. Separate packages are available for Windows x64, Linux x64, Linux ARM64 and macOS ARM64.\n\nCompatibility:\n\n* Windows 10, 11 and Windows Server 2016 to 2025 (ARM64)\n* .NET 10.0, 9.0, 8.0, 7.0, 6.0 and .NET Standard 2.0\n* .NET Framework 4.6.2 to 4.8.1\n* Azure App Service and Azure Functions for Windows\n* Docker containers for Windows\n* Web, Console and Desktop applications\n\nMain Features:\n\n* Convert HTML with CSS3, SVG, web fonts and JavaScript to PDF\n* Create PDF links, forms, bookmarks and table of contents from HTML\n* Place HTML content in PDF pages, headers and footers\n* Convert HTML to JPEG, PNG and SVG images\n* Create PDF documents with text, graphics and images\n* Set PDF security and digital signatures\n* Edit, stamp and merge PDF documents\n\nDocumentation and code samples:\nhttps://www.evopdf.com/evopdf-html-to-pdf-dotnet",
